   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2023, amending the correction law\nrelating to requiring religious dietary food options in prison commissaries\nand visitor's areas, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 4748-B and A.\n5939, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8091",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8091-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap of 2023 (as proposed in S.4748-B and A.5939)",
    "lawSection": "Correctional Services",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8091\n\nSPONSOR: RAMOS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2023, amending the correction\nlaw relating to requiring religious dietary food options in prison\ncommissaries and visitor's areas, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 4748-B and A. 5939, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to the correction law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis amendment extends the effective date to give the Department of\nCorrection and Community Supervision more time to implement this legis-\nlation.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter. The\nExecutive aimed to give the agency more time to comply with this legis-\nlation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 687 of the Laws of 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the two hundred seventieth day after it\nshall have become a law.\n",
